---
import DetailHeading from '../detailHeading.astro';
---
<div class="space-y-6 text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
  <section>
    <DetailHeading>Delivery model</DetailHeading>
    <p class="mt-4">
      The site is a content-first portfolio for Sebastian Sośniak. Astro renders the pages as mostly static output, while TypeScript keeps the components and supporting utilities type-safe. The visual layer uses Tailwind CSS and the delivered product is available at <a class="text-green-400 hover:underline" href="https://metricmind.pl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">metricmind.pl</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <DetailHeading>Implementation decisions</DetailHeading>
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
      <li><span class="font-bold text-slate-300">Static-first rendering:</span> project and experience content is prepared at build time.</li>
      <li><span class="font-bold text-slate-300">Typed components:</span> TypeScript provides a shared contract while the page grows.</li>
      <li><span class="font-bold text-slate-300">Utility styling:</span> Tailwind CSS keeps the presentation consistent without a separate bespoke style system.</li>
      <li><span class="font-bold text-slate-300">Hosting:</span> Vercel serves the live site and its public deployment path.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <DetailHeading>Evidence boundary</DetailHeading>
    <p class="mt-4">
      The public repository records 10 commits. No public analytics or conversion history is available, so the result is stated as the delivered live portfolio and its implementation choices.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
